1# Create the DynamoDB Table:

In this step, we will set up a DynamoDB table to store cloud-related definitions that our application will use.
DynamoDB is a fully managed NoSQL database provided by AWS, designed to deliver fast and predictable performance.
It is ideal for applications requiring high availability, scalability, and low latency, like our dictionary application.

Log in to the AWS Management Console.
In the search bar, type DynamoDB and select it from the list of services.
Once on the DynamoDB dashboard, click Create Table.
Table Name: Enter CloudDefinitions. This name will help identify our table in AWS.
Primary Key: Define the partition key as term (Type: String).
This key will uniquely identify each term in our dictionary, ensuring no duplicates.
Leave other options as default (such as capacity mode set to "On-demand") and click Create Table.

